# T7 — slice_mesh thin-band fix: verification log
# Date: 2026-08-10

## Changes applied
File: mcp_server/mesh_slicer.py (2 targeted fixes, 0 signature changes)

### Fix A: _triangle_plane_segment — clamp near-plane distances (L212-224)
Renamed `dists` → `raw_dists`, then created a clamped `dists` that zeroes
any distance within onplane_eps. The `on` array is computed from raw_dists
(before clamping), so on-plane-corner classification is unaffected. The
edge-crossing loop (L227-235) now uses clamped dists, so edges touching
an on-plane vertex never produce spurious crossings (0 * dj = 0, not < 0).

Before: vertex at d=9e-7 (within onplane_eps=1e-6) → edge to opposite-side
  vertex has di*dj = 9e-7 * (-0.25) < 0 → spurious crossing near vertex.
After: clamped d=0.0 → 0 * (-0.25) = 0, not < 0 → no spurious crossing.

### Fix B: _chain_loops — append first-hop vertex (L303-314)
Moved `loop.append(reps[nxt2])` (old L314) to the top of the while loop as
`loop.append(reps[cur])` (new L304). This appends the CURRENT vertex before
finding the next one, ensuring ALL loop vertices are included. The old code
only appended reps[start] and subsequent nxt2 values, skipping the first hop.

Before: 4-segment rectangle (no midpoints) → loop=[start, hop3, hop2] = 3 pts
After:  4-segment rectangle (no midpoints) → loop=[start, hop1, hop2, hop3] = 4 pts

